new Judicial Service Commission created.
● Article 111F of the Constitution spells out
the functions and powers of the JSC in relation to officers in the Singapore
Judicial Service:

a. Appointment;

b. Confirmation;

c. Emplacement on the permanent establishment;

d. Promotion;

e. Transfer;

f. Disciplinary control; and

g. Dismissal.

The JSC supervises all judicial officers in the
State Courts, including judges and assistant registrars. Legal Service officers
(eg prosecutors and parliamentary draftsmen) remain under the purview of the
Legal Service Commission.
